//! WHAT A LINEAR ROUTE SCAN COSTS as the table grows, and what the
//! COMPILED TABLE costs on the same routes — measured in one program
//! so the two answers share a machine and a minute. Every
//! measurement hits the LAST route in the table, which is the
//! scan's worst case and the table's best argument.
//!
//! THREE SHAPES, because a table of distinct first segments is the
//! one case a one-level index would already win: `deep` shares a
//! prefix so the deciding step is the third, and `wild` opens with a
//! HOLE so every route stays live past step one.
//!
//! GENERATED by `generate.py` beside this file.
